From 2388814244b9a3c25962fa7d28d9048de8c77ab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:41:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/24] libos/linux: Make abort override a blocked or ignored
 SIGABRT

POSIX: abort overrides blocking or ignoring SIGABRT, and the status is
that of a process terminated by SIGABRT. The generic abort raised the
signal and then called _exit(1), so a blocked or ignored SIGABRT, or a
handler that returned, gave exit status 1. Unblock SIGABRT, raise it,
and if that returns restore the default action and raise it again.
---
 libos/linux/abort.c     | 67 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libos/linux/meson.build |  1 +
 2 files changed, 68 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libos/linux/abort.c

